---
description: Brightside design-system rules for UI work
globs: src/**/*.tsx, src/app/globals.css
alwaysApply: false
---

Follow the rules in @AGENTS.md. In short:

- Use only the semantic tokens in `src/app/globals.css`. There is no default Tailwind palette, no arbitrary values and no inline styles.
- Reuse components from `src/components/ui/` before you create new ones.
- Every component has a story that covers its key states. Accessibility violations fail CI.
- Work on a branch and open a pull request. `main` deploys to production.
- Before you finish a change, run `pnpm lint && pnpm typecheck && pnpm test:stories`.
- Each step of a contribution has written instructions in `.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md` (`start-change`, `preview-locally`, `design-review`, `explain-diff`, `finish-work`, `create-pr`, `address-review`). When the user asks for one of those steps, read that file and follow it.
